Subject: telnet/telnetd: explicitly include <sys/select.h>

Several translation units (telnet/utilities, telnet/tn3270,
telnetd/telnetd, telnetd/utility) use fd_set / FD_ZERO / FD_SET /
select() but rely on the historical glibc/BSD-libc behavior of
pulling <sys/select.h> in transitively from <sys/types.h> or
<sys/time.h>.  Substrate keeps those headers strictly separated
(adding the include creates mutual recursion: sys/select.h →
sys/time.h → sys/select.h).  Add the explicit include — once in
telnetd's shared umbrella header (covers telnetd.c + utility.c)
and once each in the standalone telnet TUs.

---
diff -urN a/telnet/tn3270.c b/telnet/tn3270.c
--- a/telnet/tn3270.c
+++ b/telnet/tn3270.c
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 #include <config.h>

 #include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/select.h>
 #include <arpa/telnet.h>

 #include "general.h"
diff -urN a/telnet/utilities.c b/telnet/utilities.c
--- a/telnet/utilities.c
+++ b/telnet/utilities.c
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/socket.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
+#include <sys/select.h>
 #include <time.h>
 #include <ctype.h>

diff -urN a/telnetd/telnetd.h b/telnetd/telnetd.h
--- a/telnetd/telnetd.h
+++ b/telnetd/telnetd.h
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <config.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
+#include <sys/select.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
